  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> be a non-zero real number. Suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is a differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to ________.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2SBSL",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
